   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A fully operational  CUVECOM and &#x201c;Kunene Commission  joint secretariat that is able to  coordinate initiatives, institutions  and International Cooperating  Partners (ICPs) in a harmonized  manner and promote IWRM  principles in the Cuvelai and Kunene  River Basins.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A fully operational  CUVECOM and &#x201c;Kunene Commission  joint secretariat that is able to  coordinate initiatives, institutions  and International Cooperating  Partners (ICPs) in a harmonized  manner and promote IWRM  principles in the Cuvelai and Kunene  River Basins.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2024">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- CUVECOM has established a Secretariat with 5 full-time staff, Head office in Oshakati and a satellite office in Ondjiva. The 
CUVECOM Council and Technical Task Team (TTT) both 
meet on a regular basis. CUVECOM has a website and 
accessible resources but there is no information management 
system to share available data and information
- Kunene Basin has no Commission or Secretariat, the transboundary PJTC meets 
regularly</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2030-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2030-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Cuvelai Watercourse Commission (CUVECOM) fully capacitated and sustainable 
- Permanent Joint Technical Commission (PJTC) transformed 
into Kunene Commission and sustainable
- Joint secretariat fully functional and sustainable
- 100 % of personnel within Intergovernmental institutional structure trained in Gender Equality Capacity needs.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Cuvelai Watercourse Commission (CUVECOM) fully capacitated and sustainable 
- Permanent Joint Technical Commission (PJTC) transformed 
into Kunene Commission and sustainable
- Joint secretariat fully functional and sustainable</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Critical knowledge gaps  filled in the following areas to  support joint planning and analysis  of the Kunene River Basin: &#x2022; Ecological water requirements &#x2022; Sediment transport &#x2022; Future water resources  development &#x2022; Hydropower development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Critical knowledge gaps  filled in the following areas to  support joint planning and analysis  of the Kunene River Basin: &#x2022; Ecological water requirements &#x2022; Sediment transport &#x2022; Future water resources  development &#x2022; Hydropower development</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2024">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Ecological flow requirements not evaluated or only partially identified
- Very limited data on sediment transport 
- Water resources development plans exist and some systems analysis has been carried out at national levels.
- Rapid analysis and identification of gaps completed under GIZ support (2022/23) .
The rest of the baseline data are in the baseline notes due to character limit</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2030-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2030-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved knowledge of groundwater in both countries following BGR Phase 2 study 60% of sustainable potential identified with confidence
- Flood risk mapping established
-  Transboundary Flood early warning system fully functional
- 50% of those managing EWS are women
The rest of the Target data are in the target notes due to character limit</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">TORs for consultancy signed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
